# How to cite NetSimR; GitHub shows it as "Cite this repository". The R citation is
# inst/CITATION (citation("NetSimR")). Keep the version that of DESCRIPTION
# (tests/testthat/test-citation-cff.R checks it).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NetSimR, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "NetSimR: Actuarial Functions for Non-Life Insurance Modelling"
abstract: >-
  An R package of actuarial functions for non-life insurance and reinsurance pricing,
  reserving and capital modelling, with six Shiny tools for simulating claims, fitting
  distributions and generalised linear models, reserving, pricing excess of loss
  reinsurance and the capital of a portfolio, which also run in the browser.
authors:
  - given-names: Yiannis
    family-names: Parizas
    email: yiannis.parizas@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-0523-0751"
version: 0.4.0
license: GPL-3.0-only
url: "https://netsimanalytics.github.io/NetSimR/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/NetSimAnalytics/NetSimR"
repository-artifact: "https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=NetSimR"
keywords:
  - actuarial science
  - non-life insurance
  - reinsurance
  - claims reserving
  - pricing
  - capital modelling
  - R
  - Shiny
